are more shortages (about 90 units of product 1, roughly 26 lost per unit). This comes out about even with 1.1×, so candidate 1 is close to candidate 0.\n- Candidate 3 is candidate 0 with smaller final orders, so less stock is left over at the end. That puts it slightly ahead of candidate 0.\n\n**Batched orders.** Ordering less often saves the fixed 31 per order day, but the bigger batches mean more stock held on average:\n- Candidate 6 (every 2 days) saves about 400 in order fees and pays about 600 more in storage, a net of about −200 versus candidate 0.\n- Candidate 2 (every 3 days) saves about 500 and pays about 1,200 more in storage, a net of about −700. It may also lose some stock to the 208-unit capacity limit.\n\n**Estimated order:** 3 > 0 ≈ 1 > 6 > 2 > 4 > 7 > 5."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5050, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5050}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:21:36.597Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWCfNpwys1jCTSG5oy5a"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01PTokjwyU8cAn1jdzHYtjpu", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWCfP5b3rFiL9d8Rdk55", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01PTokjwyU8cAn1jdzHYtjpu", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {"p": [0.75, 0.62, 0.42, 0.8, 0.3, 0.